# Frontend Conventions

- Vite + React 19, plain JSX (no TypeScript). Functional components only.
- `vite.config.js` sets `build.outDir: 'build'` — do not change; the deployment
  flow uploads `frontend/build/` to the server html directory.
- Dev server proxies `/api` to `http://localhost:5000` (Express backend).
- Site content is fetched from `/api/content` at runtime via `ContentProvider`
  (`src/data/ContentContext.jsx`); components read it with `useContent()` —
  never hard-code business content (names, prices, schedules, links) inside
  components and never import content statically. `src/data/siteContent.js`
  holds the bundled default content (fallback while loading / backend down)
  plus `deriveContent()` (builds hero eyebrow and program registration links);
  it must stay in the same shape as `backend/data/content.default.json`.
- One component per page section in `src/components/`, each importing its own
  co-located CSS file. Page assembly happens in `App.jsx`.
- `/admin` renders `src/admin/AdminApp.jsx` (path branch in `main.jsx`, no
  router): password login → JWT in sessionStorage → per-section forms →
  `PUT /api/content`. Reusable form fields live in `src/admin/fields.jsx`,
  section editors in `src/admin/sections/`, API calls in `src/admin/api.js`.
- Staff coach objects may include an optional `image` URL and a
  `photoVisibility` value from 0–100 (default 50). The Staff admin editor
  uploads portraits immediately through `/api/admin/coach-images` and provides
  a per-coach visibility slider with a live preview; the normal content Save
  persists both values. Public staff cards use the portrait as a full-card
  background beneath the coach-specific dark overlay and show a branded
  watermark when no image exists or an image cannot load.
- Assistant coach accolades use `accoladeGroups: [{ label, items }]`, editable
  with the same add/remove/reorder group controls used for the head coach.
  Rendering and the admin editor retain a fallback for legacy assistant
  `accolades: string[]` content until that coach's groups are saved.
- Program objects may include `image` and `imageVisibility` (0–100, default 50).
  The Programs admin editor uploads wide photos through
  `/api/admin/program-images` and provides a per-program live visibility
  preview. Public program cards render the photo beneath a dark overlay; cards
  without images retain the standard brown background.
- Hero content may include `image` and `imageVisibility` (0–100, default 50).
  The Hero admin editor uploads wide photos through `/api/admin/hero-images`
  and provides a live tint preview. The public hero retains its fixed
  left-side readability gradient and uses the bundled wrestling image whenever
  no custom image is configured.
- Footer navigation is content-driven through `footer.groups`, where each group
  has a title and reorderable `{ label, href }` links. The `/admin` Footer
  section manages groups and links; legacy live content without `footer` uses
  the bundled defaults until footer changes are saved.
- Linting: `npm run lint` (oxlint).
- Reviews currently persist to localStorage (`agoge-reviews` key) and the contact
  form falls back to mailto. Both have TODOs to switch to `/api/reviews` and
  `/api/contact` when the backend is wired up.
